cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use DarcyWarp in your work, cite the paper below and record the exact
  software commit or release, formulation, solver and precision used. The paper
  describes the original steady, fixed-transmissivity implementation.
type: software
title: "DarcyWarp: two-dimensional groundwater flow on CPUs and NVIDIA GPUs"
authors:
  - family-names: Durney
    given-names: Patrick
  - family-names: Fourie
    given-names: Jaco
repository-code: "https://github.com/Lincoln-Environmental/DarcyWarp"
url: "https://github.com/Lincoln-Environmental/DarcyWarp"
abstract: >-
  DarcyWarp provides two-dimensional confined and unconfined groundwater flow
  solvers implemented with NVIDIA Warp, with steady and transient formulations,
  CPU and CUDA execution, numerical comparison workflows and ensemble benchmarks.
keywords:
  - groundwater
  - Darcy flow
  - numerical modelling
  - GPU computing
  - NVIDIA Warp
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  authors:
    - family-names: Durney
      given-names: Patrick
    - family-names: Fourie
      given-names: Jaco
  title: >-
    DarcyWarp: A graphics processing unit (GPU)-accelerated multigrid solver
    for repeated 2D fixed-transmissivity groundwater solves validated against
    reference solvers
  journal: "Environmental Modelling & Software"
  year: 2026
  volume: "204"
  start: "107081"
  doi: "10.1016/j.envsoft.2026.107081"
